--TEST--
`Core\Cli\Text::text` answers the text of every run joined and leaves the styling out — `rule:tooling/styling-is-a-value-not-a-grammar`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A `Text` holds runs — a body and the `Cli\Style` that body wears — so reading
// one answers what it says rather than how it will look. That holds whether or
// not the stream it would be written to is a terminal, which is why this case
// can assert it while every stream here is piped.
var $style = Core\Cli\Style::of({color: Core\Cli\Color::RED, bold: true});
var $warn = Core\Cli\Text::styled("careful", $style);
echo $warn->text(), "\n";

// Composition joins runs, so the text of a sum is its operands' texts in order,
// and a styled operand contributes its body alone.
var $whole = $warn + Core\Cli\Text::plain(": ") + Core\Cli\Text::plain("check the path");
echo $whole->text(), "\n";

// The empty carrier reads as the empty string, not as `null`.
var $empty = Core\Cli\Text::plain("");
echo "[", $empty->text(), "]\n";
--EXPECT--
careful
careful: check the path
[]
